CWTS multi-institution strings

The 952 strings in strings.jsonl.gz were selected by CWTS, the Centre for Science and Technology Studies at
Leiden University. CWTS chose strings that name two or more institutions and listed the institutions it saw
in each. OpenAlex labelled them with OpenAlex institution ids in 2023. Credit for the curation belongs to CWTS.

Original release: OurResearch published the set in 2023 as two of the test sets for OpenAlex's V2
institution parser:

  https://github.com/ourresearch/openalex-institution-parsing/tree/main/V2 (README, "Test Data")
  files cwts_related_labeled.tsv (823 rows) and cwts_no_relation_labeled.tsv (182 rows), inside
  institution_gold_datasets_v2.tgz in the public bucket s3://openalex-institution-tagger-model-artifacts/V2/
  (uploaded 29 March 2023), also in the public Google Sheet "OpenAlex Benchmark Data" linked from that README

The two files hold 1,005 rows and 952 distinct strings; strings.jsonl.gz has one row per distinct string,
numbered in order of first appearance (the related file first).

License: no license was attached to the data files. The repository's code is under the MIT License
(Copyright (c) 2022 OurResearch). The strings are affiliation strings as printed in published papers, and the
labels are OpenAlex ids (CC0). We redistribute the set here, unchanged apart from the fields OpenAlex added
(ROR ids for the labels, the 2023 system's, the new matcher's and ROR's matcher's answers), with credit to CWTS.

One change to the labels: two institution ids in the 2023 labels have since been merged into other records
(I4210092866 into I4210094082, I4210125713 into I1294278766). "labels" uses the current records;
"labels_as_released" keeps the 2023 ids.
